faqs:
  - q: "How long does a Salesforce to HubSpot migration take?"
    a: "Our migrations typically take three to six weeks. The range depends on data volume, how many objects and custom objects are in scope, the number of integrations, and how much Salesforce automation has to be rebuilt as HubSpot workflows."
  - q: "Can we keep our activity history from Salesforce?"
    a: "Yes, where it matters. The source audit decides which tasks, events, emails, and notes come across and which are archived outside HubSpot. The mapping sheet records how each activity type is imported and which records it is associated with."
  - q: "Should we run Salesforce and HubSpot in parallel?"
    a: "Keep the overlap as short as possible. A long parallel run means two sources of truth and data entered twice. We prefer a short freeze window: stop edits in Salesforce, run the final delta import, reconcile, then switch the team over with Salesforce kept read-only for reference."
  - q: "Can HubSpot and Salesforce stay in sync instead of migrating?"
    a: "Yes. If Salesforce stays for part of the business, a bi-directional sync with clear field ownership and deduplication may fit better than a full migration. See our <a href=\"/integrations/\">HubSpot integration services</a> for how we design that."
